'''Portal de Sant Cristòfor Station''' is a major multi-level railway and metro interchange station in [[Original (ciutat)|Original]], [[Sant Cristòfor]], [[Balboa]]. Located approximately 3 km south of the [[Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal]], the station is a multi-tenant complex combining underground metro services, an elevated commuter and high-speed rail station, a commercial department store, and office space across two towers. The station is situated adjacent to the [[Estadi de Balboa]], the national stadium, and serves as the primary rail access point for the stadium complex during events.

The station serves [[CristoCarril]] [[Line B (CristoCarril)|Line B]], [[Line C (CristoCarril)|Line C]], [[Line D (CristoCarril)|Line D]], and [[Line E (CristoCarril)|Line E]] commuter rail services on its elevated level, with 16 platforms. High-speed rail services on the [[Sant Cristòfor–Portnou HSR line]] serve the station on a limited basis during events at the Estadi de Balboa. Below ground, the station serves [[Metro de Sant Cristòfor|Metro]] [[Metro de Sant Cristòfor|Lines 2 and 4]], providing connections across the Original district and to neighbouring ciutats including [[Dàrsena (ciutat)|Dàrsena]], [[Sant Martí (ciutat)|Sant Martí]], and [[Ciutat de l'Estació (ciutat)|Ciutat de l'Estació]].

== History ==

The original station at Portal de Sant Cristòfor was constructed as a cut-and-cover metro station for [[Metro de Sant Cristòfor|Metro]] Line 2 during the Zong era, when Lines 1 and 2 were built to serve the Original district. The cut-and-cover method involved excavating a shallow trench from the surface, constructing the station box, and covering it over, resulting in a station at shallow depth beneath street level.

When Metro Line 4 was constructed during the post-reunification era, its tunnels were bored at a greater depth beneath the existing Line 2 station. An atrium was constructed between the Line 2 and Line 4 levels to facilitate passenger movement between the two metro lines. In the original configuration, passengers accessing Line 4 from the surface were required to descend to the Line 2 level, proceed through the atrium, and then continue down to the Line 4 level.

The station underwent a major reconstruction in 2007 as part of the broader Sant Cristòfor high-speed rail project, which also included the construction of the adjacent [[Estadi de Balboa]]. The rebuilding created the elevated rail station with 16 platforms above the existing underground metro infrastructure and added a second atrium on a northwest–southeast axis, equipped with high-speed elevators providing direct connections between the underground metro levels, the ground-floor commercial concourse, and the elevated rail station. This second atrium eliminated the need for passengers to pass through the Line 2 level when transferring between the surface and Line 4, though the original atrium remains in use for Line 2–Line 4 transfers.

The above-ground complex was constructed with two towers oriented on a northwest–southeast axis, housing commercial and office space above the station concourse. The ground level of the complex accommodates an HRX department store, with office space occupying levels 4 through 12 of the towers.

== Layout ==

Portal de Sant Cristòfor Station is a multi-level complex extending from underground metro tunnels to elevated rail platforms and commercial towers. The station is oriented roughly north–south for the rail and metro alignments, with the commercial complex and second atrium aligned on a northwest–southeast axis.

=== Underground: Metro levels ===

The below-ground portion of the station consists of four tracks in two separated tunnels, carrying [[Metro de Sant Cristòfor|Metro]] Lines 2 and 4 in a north–south alignment.

Line 2 occupies the upper underground level, constructed using the cut-and-cover method at shallow depth beneath the street. The Line 2 station has two tracks serving a single island platform. Line 2 runs from [[Sant Martí (ciutat)|Sant Martí]] through Original to [[Ciutat de l'Estació (ciutat)|Ciutat de l'Estació]], providing east–west connectivity across the central districts of Sant Cristòfor.

Line 4 occupies the lower underground level, constructed using bored tunnels at greater depth beneath the Line 2 station. The Line 4 station has two tracks serving a single island platform. Line 4 runs from [[Dàrsena (ciutat)|Dàrsena]] through Original to [[Mare de Déu del Mar]], providing connectivity between the waterfront districts and the eastern coast.

The original atrium, constructed when Line 4 was built, connects the Line 2 and Line 4 levels and remains the primary transfer route between the two metro lines. A second atrium, added during the 2007 reconstruction, is aligned on a northwest–southeast axis and is equipped with high-speed elevators providing direct vertical circulation between the underground metro levels, the ground-floor concourse, and the elevated rail station. This second atrium allows passengers to bypass the Line 2 level when travelling between the surface and Line 4, and provides a direct connection from both metro levels to the elevated rail platforms.

=== Ground level: Commercial concourse ===

The ground level of the station complex houses the main passenger concourse, ticket halls, and fare gates for the elevated rail station, as well as the entrance to the underground metro station. The ground level also contains an HRX department store, integrated into the station complex as part of the 2007 redevelopment.

=== Elevated: Rail station ===

The elevated rail station, situated above the ground-level concourse, has 16 platforms serving [[CristoCarril]] commuter rail services. The platforms are arranged on a northwest–southeast alignment, following the orientation of the above-ground complex. The elevated station serves CristoCarril [[Line B (CristoCarril)|Line B]], [[Line C (CristoCarril)|Line C]], [[Line D (CristoCarril)|Line D]], and [[Line E (CristoCarril)|Line E]] under regular operation. During events at the [[Estadi de Balboa]], the station is additionally served by high-speed rail services on the [[Sant Cristòfor–Portnou HSR line]], which make a special stop at Portal de Sant Cristòfor to provide direct high-speed connections from the [[Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal]] and from [[Varakí TDV (CristoCarril)|Varakí TDV]].

=== Towers and offices ===

The above-ground complex includes two towers oriented on a northwest–southeast axis, rising above the elevated rail station and commercial concourse. Office space occupies levels 4 through 12 of the towers, with the lower levels accommodating station operations, retail, and the HRX department store.

== Services ==

=== CristoCarril ===

Portal de Sant Cristòfor is served by four [[CristoCarril]] lines on the elevated station:

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Line !! Direction !! Service patterns
|-
| [[Line B (CristoCarril)|Line B]] | [[Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal]] ↔ [[Estació Central de Portnou|Portnou]] | Short, Limited, Express, Local
|-
| [[Line C (CristoCarril)|Line C]] | [[Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal]] ↔ [[Varakí Central (CristoCarril)|Varakí Central]] | Short, Express, Local
|-
| [[Line D (CristoCarril)|Line D]] | — | —
|-
| [[Line E (CristoCarril)|Line E]] | — | —
|}

Lines B and C share the first four stations south of the Central Terminal, with Portal de Sant Cristòfor as the second station on both lines. Line B diverges at [[La Font (CristoCarril)|La Font]] to follow the [[Portnou Line]] corridor through [[Dàrsena (ciutat)|Dàrsena]] and [[Sant Llorenç (ciutat)|Sant Llorenç]], while Line C continues on the [[Varakí Line]] corridor through the eastern ciutats.

=== High-speed rail ===

High-speed rail services on the [[Sant Cristòfor–Portnou HSR line]] serve Portal de Sant Cristòfor only during events at the [[Estadi de Balboa]]. The event service adds approximately 2 minutes to the end-to-end HSR journey time and is scheduled around the event timetable, with increased service frequency before and after events to manage crowd movements.

=== Metro ===

The underground station serves [[Metro de Sant Cristòfor|Metro]] Lines 2 and 4:

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Line !! Direction
|-
| [[Metro de Sant Cristòfor|Line 2]] | [[Sant Martí (ciutat)|Sant Martí]] ↔ [[Ciutat de l'Estació (ciutat)|Ciutat de l'Estació]]
|-
| [[Metro de Sant Cristòfor|Line 4]] | [[Dàrsena (ciutat)|Dàrsena]] ↔ [[Mare de Déu del Mar]]
|}

The metro station is integrated with the [[Tarifa Integrada]] fare system, allowing free transfers to CristoCarril and other transport services within a 90-minute window.

== Role in the network ==

Portal de Sant Cristòfor Station functions as a key interchange between the underground metro network and the elevated commuter and high-speed rail network in southern Original. The station's multi-level design, with the second atrium and high-speed elevators, was specifically engineered to handle large passenger surges during events at the adjacent Estadi de Balboa, enabling rapid distribution of crowds between the elevated rail platforms, the metro levels, and the surface.

The station's commercial components — the HRX department store and office towers — were integrated into the 2007 redevelopment as part of a transit-oriented development strategy, generating revenue to support the station's operation and creating a mixed-use complex that serves both transit passengers and the surrounding neighbourhood.

